title: Pillar 0 advisory tier shipped (v6.8.0) — team-invocation graduates to the hook tier
summary: 'Implemented the invocation-reliability ladder from strategy TD-2026-06-10-101: prompt-gate (UserPromptSubmit, decision-time directive injected into model context once per TTL window, telemetry every match), team edit-gate (PreToolUse Write|Edit one-time advisory), paradigm solo CLI with enumerated reasons, deduped bypass events in stop-hook Check 13, #team-funnel core module computing invocation + legible rates surfaced in doctor. Reviewer pass caught the decisive bug pre-ship: the Stop hook fires per assistant TURN not per session, so stop-clearing markers would have erased solo declarations mid-session, re-nagged every turn, and double-counted bypasses — fix is TTL-based marker expiry (PARADIGM_GATE_TTL_HOURS, default 4h), verified by aging markers in smoke tests. Loid pre-ratified the telemetry design and the anti-distortion rule (advisory-first 4 weeks; hollow invocations must be quarantined from expertise before any blocking tier). Also discovered: the v6.0 deprecation error recommends ''paradigm decision record'' which was never built as a CLI command (MCP-only) — same bug class as dealoracle''s report; decision TD-2026-06-10-101 was hand-written to the store as the workaround. 386+290 tests green.'
